cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MSS Drum Fidelity Evaluation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ding
    given-names: Chuxin
    affiliation: "Universitat Autònoma de Barcelona"
    email: chuxinding@outlook.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3508-4120"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dingchuxin/MSS_drum_fidelity_eval"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-12"
abstract: >-
  Code and per-track results for a study of what separated drum stems can and cannot
  be trusted for in microrhythm analysis. Four open separators (Spleeter, HT-Demucs,
  BS-RoFormer and SCNet-XL) separate the 50 tracks of the MUSDB18-HQ test set, and
  every measurement (onset timing, stroke levels, envelope shape, developer metrics) is
  made on the estimated and on the true drum stem with the same code and settings; the
  difference, estimate minus reference, is reported for each track.
keywords:
  - music source separation
  - music information retrieval
  - rhythm
  - microtiming
  - evaluation
  - MUSDB18
  - onset detection
